implementationPlan.description:
Prove the hunt repro end to end in reportBlocked.test.ts. Edit tool only.
- Where: in the first `describe('moe.report_blocked')` block, the one with the addWorker/report/mentionedGeneralPosts helpers. Insert a nested describe, "on the launchers' role-less project team (team role, then id prefix)", directly before the case 'always posts to #governors, with or without a live architect'.
- Import: add `import { resolveWorkerRole } from '../util/workerRole.js';` right under the existing workerLiveness import.
- Do not edit addWorker or any existing case.

Local helper addProjectTeamSeat(workerId, secondsAgo):
- reuse the one role-less team named 'moes', calling state.createTeam({ name: 'moes' }) the first time;
- createWorker exactly as addWorker does, then addTeamMember;
- THEN stamp lastActivityAt, because addTeamMember bumps it (mem:gotcha-daemon-team-membership-and-freshness).

Case 1 (DoD 1, the hunt #16 repro):
- call addProjectTeamSeat('architect-2a219562', 5);
- assert resolveWorkerRole(state, 'architect-2a219562') is 'architect';
- call report() and assert task-1 is BLOCKED;
- notified toEqual { target: 'architect-2a219562', via: 'freshest-live-architect' };
- message toBe 'Task blocked; seat freed — this response does not start another task session. Pinged architect-2a219562 (freshest live architect).';
- exactly one mentioned #general post, matching /^@architect-2a219562 🚧 worker-1 blocked on task-1: npm install fails behind the proxy$/;
- rolePosts toEqual [['architects', paged], ['governors', paged.slice('@architect-2a219562 '.length)]].
Do NOT copy the repro's `c.slice(0, 60)` literals from /mnt/d/moe-scratch/hunt-151a2c54/B. They are mis-sized because 🚧 is two UTF-16 code units, so they fail even with the fix. Assert whole strings or anchored regexes as above.

Case 2 (with no live architect the ping still escalates to the governors):
- addProjectTeamSeat('architect-stale', LIVENESS_TIMEOUT_MS / 1000 + 60);
- addProjectTeamSeat('architect-dead', 2), then updateWorker('architect-dead', { status: 'DEAD' });
- call report();
- notified toEqual { target: '@governors', via: 'governors-fallback' };
- the rolePosts roles toEqual ['governors'], and that copy matches /^@governors 🚧 worker-1 blocked on task-1: /.

Case 1 fails on the unfixed selector. Case 2 passes either way: it pins the escalation test coverage. No production code changes in this step; reportBlocked.ts stays untouched because its call site (:405-433) already routes a non-null result to the architect page.

Sync the contract. Edit tool only.
- Where: in docs/MCP_SERVER.md `### moe.report_blocked`, edit ONLY the `- **Ping routing:**` bullet. Find it by its text; it was at :1241 at b9205914 and moves as other rows land.
- What: replace the clause 'resolving the role through `worker.teamId`.' with the team-role-then-id-prefix rule. Keep the exact phrase 'team role first, then the id prefix', because the gate greps for it on the Ping routing line.
- Verified wording: '…resolving the role through `worker.teamId`, team role first, then the id prefix: a seat whose team has a `role` takes that role, so an `architect-…` seat on a `worker` team is never paged, and a seat whose team has no role (the launchers put every architect, worker and QA seat on one role-less project team) counts as an architect when its id starts with `architect-`. A seat with no team, or whose team no longer exists, is not paged.' The existing sentences that start 'The blocked worker itself is excluded' then continue unchanged.
- Leave everything else untouched:
  - the '- With **no live architect**' bullet;
  - the Stale-block visibility bullet (task-590b98bd owns it);
  - the Returns block;
  - the governors auto-push line that quotes '🚧 {worker} blocked on {taskId}';
  - every other section.
- Check: `git diff -- docs/MCP_SERVER.md` must show one hunk with one changed line (DoD 3).

Verification. After steps 1-3, run this exact command once from the worktree root. It is the moe.complete_task verification command, and QA re-runs it:
( set -o pipefail; cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" && grep -c 'Ping routing:.*team role first, then the id prefix' docs/MCP_SERVER.md && L=$(mktemp -d) && git archive HEAD | tar -x -C "$L" && cp --parents packages/moe-daemon/src/{util/workerLiveness{,.test}.ts,tools/reportBlocked.test.ts} "$L/" && cd "$L/packages/moe-daemon" && printf '{"extends":"./tsconfig.json","include":["src/util/workerLiveness.test.ts","src/tools/reportBlocked.test.ts"],"exclude":[]}' > tt.json && env -i HOME="$HOME" NO_COLOR=1 PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" bash -c 'npm ci && npx tsc --noEmit && npx tsc -p tt.json --noEmit && npx vitest run src/util/worker{Liveness,Role}.test.ts src/tools/reportBlocked.test.ts' > ../v.log 2>&1 || { echo "$L"; tail -40 ../v.log; exit 1; }; grep -aE '^ +(Test Files|Tests) | ✓ src/' ../v.log; grep -aq 'workerLiveness\.test\.ts (2[1-9] tests' ../v.log && grep -aq 'reportBlocked\.test\.ts (6[5-9] tests' ../v.log && echo PINNED )

What it does, in order:
- greps the Ping routing rule;
- archives HEAD into a temp dir and copies the three edited code/test files over it;
- runs npm ci;
- runs the project typecheck, then a typecheck of the two test files (tt.json, because tsconfig excludes tests);
- runs vitest on workerLiveness, workerRole and reportBlocked.

Expected output: '1', workerLiveness 21 tests, workerRole 6, reportBlocked 65, 3 files and 92 tests passed, then PINNED, exit 0.
- On failure it prints the temp dir and the log tail. A bare '0' with exit 1 means the docs phrase is missing.
- Never run npm in packages/ of the shared checkout or of the worktree (global rail): this command runs everything in /tmp.
- Keep NO_COLOR=1: vitest colors its summary even when redirected, which breaks the greps.
- Do not lengthen the command: it is 980 chars, and a checkRef is capped at 1000.
